        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fancher%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1949, the hamlet unveiled a clock‑tower memorial of Medina sandstone, honoring ten local soldiers who died in World War II.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/fancher_new_york"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Nestled in western New York, Fancher sits within the Town of Murray, just seven miles north of Lake Ontario and beside the historic Erie Canal.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fancher%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Medina sandstone quarried in Fancher was shipped via the Erie Canal and New York Central Railroad, fueling regional construction in the 1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        9,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fancher%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Fancher World War II Memorial earned a spot on both the New York State and National Historic Registers in 2022.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
